Adds the claude.com self-service-analytics post: (D1) the "silent failure" —
plausible-but-wrong, single correct answer with no deterministic oracle, "we don't
have a robust solution yet" = Carnot's exact problem in its hardest (facts-like,
no-oracle) regime; (D2) a real accuracy/cost Pareto datapoint (adversarial review
+6% acc / +72% latency; cheaper-judge loses the win; structure>access echoes the
Sudoku finding); (D3) context-engineering 21%->95% + maintenance decay = conductor
reliability lesson. Single-pass quotes, flagged for two-pass verify. Mirrors the
hybrid-pragmatic-architecture memory's Pareto calibration.

